.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-delete - Delete a message (soft delete)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams delete  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a message the way Teams does: a soft delete, which keeps the id and
leaves a tombstone in the conversation
(refs/graph/api-reference/v1.0/api/chatmessage-softdelete.md).

.PP
A chat message is deleted through the user-relative route the docs document
(POST /users/{user-id}/chats/{chat-id}/messages/{id}/softDelete), because the
/chats form answers 405 (docs/spike/phase1.md:99).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the Graph request without sending it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team the channel belongs to, when the reference does not say


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


